<title>UK: LME copper steady in late trading.</title>
<headline>LME copper steady in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper held at unchanged levels on Thursday evening in late inter-office trading after earlier failing to break through the $2,400 level.</p>
<p>At 1800 GMT, three months copper was indicated at $2,366/70 compared to a kerb close of $2,368.</p>
<p>The cash/threes backwardation was firm, last indicated at $200/$210.</p>
<p>The other metals were also little changed.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
